  "voiceName": "George (stand-in for Elderon)",
  "chapters": {
    "ch1": {
      "track": "/audio/brief/narration/ch1.mp3?v=66e76633b1bc",
      "trackHash": "66e76633b1bc",
      "duration": 27.66,
      "voiceName": "Elderon (recorded by hand)",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Your objective: understand how one treaty set the world on fire.",
          "start": 0.06,
          "end": 4.42
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn what the Treaty of Versailles demanded of Germany.",
          "start": 5.26,
          "end": 8.16
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how those terms broke a nation, and left its people desperate.",
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 12.92
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how that desperation carried Adolf Hitler to power.",
          "start": 13.9,
          "end": 16.94
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how the world watched him take land, step by step, and did nothing.",
          "start": 17.76,
          "end": 21.5
        },
        {
          "text": "And learn how it ended — with German tanks crossing into Poland.",
          "start": 22.12,
          "end": 25.58
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you accept the mission?",
          "start": 26.26,
          "end": 27.34
        }
      ]
    },
    "ch2": {
      "track": "/audio/brief/narration/ch2.mp3?v=dfa415dafb5f",
      "trackHash": "dfa415dafb5f",
      "duration": 27.4,
      "voiceName": "Elderon (recorded by hand)",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Your objective: understand the summer Britain stood alone.",
          "start": 0.06,
          "end": 4.68
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how three hundred thousand soldiers escaped from Dunkirk.",
          "start": 5.3,
          "end": 8.7
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how France surrendered — and left Britain to fight on alone.",
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 12.8
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how Eagle Day began Germany's assault from the sky.",
          "start": 13.62,
          "end": 16.8
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how the bombers turned on the cities, and the cities burned.",
          "start": 17.48,
          "end": 20.76
        },
        {
          "text": "And learn how the battle was won — and the invasion never came.",
          "start": 21.3,
          "end": 24.7
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you accept the mission?",
          "start": 26.02,
          "end": 27.04
        }
      ]
    },
    "ch3": {
      "track": "/audio/brief/narration/ch3.mp3?v=f297e78d3cc2",
      "trackHash": "f297e78d3cc2",
      "duration": 18.92,
      "voiceName": "Elderon (recorded by hand)",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Your objective: understand how the war became the whole world's war.",
          "start": 0.02,
          "end": 3.94
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn why Japan chose to strike America across the Pacific.",
          "start": 4.7,
          "end": 8.04
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn what the bombers came for at Pearl Harbor — and what they missed.",
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 12.42
        },
        {
          "text": "And learn how America's answer changed the course of the entire war.",
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 16.46
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you accept the mission?",
          "start": 17.3,
          "end": 18.58
        }
      ]
    },
    "ch4": {
      "track": "/audio/brief/narration/ch4.mp3?v=5d2334c6b04e",
      "trackHash": "5d2334c6b04e",
      "duration": 26.46,
      "voiceName": "Elderon (recorded by hand)",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Your objective: understand the battle that turned the war around.",
          "start": 0.1,
          "end": 3.66
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how Germany broke its promise and invaded the Soviet Union.",
          "start": 4.36,
          "end": 7.92
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn why the fighting came to one city on the Volga.",
          "start": 8.78,
          "end": 11.6
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how a city in ruins was defended, house by house.",
          "start": 12.24,
          "end": 15.58
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how the Red Army struck where the Germans were weakest.",
          "start": 16.4,
          "end": 19.28
        },
        {
          "text": "And learn how an entire German army was lost, and the war changed direction.",
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 24.28
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you accept the mission?",
          "start": 24.94,
          "end": 26.18
        }
      ]
    },
    "ch5": {
      "track": "/audio/brief/narration/ch5.mp3?v=34e2baae49eb",
      "trackHash": "34e2baae49eb",
      "duration": 28.42,
      "voiceName": "Elderon (recorded by hand)",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Your objective: understand how the Allies fought their way back into Europe.",
          "start": 0.08,
          "end": 4.22
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn why the Allies had to return to Western Europe at all, and what was waiting for them on that coast.",
          "start": 4.72,
          "end": 10.12
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how Britain became a launch pad, and how the whole invasion came down to a weather forecast.",
          "start": 11.06,
          "end": 16.48
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn how Germany was persuaded to look the wrong way.",
          "start": 17.46,
          "end": 20.32
        },
        {
          "text": "Learn what happened on the 6th of June, and why holding the ground mattered more than taking it.",
          "start": 20.86,
          "end": 25.94
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you accept the mission?",
          "start": 26.94,
          "end": 28.04
        }
      ]
    },
